        "heading": "Figure 10 Open in figure viewer PowerPoint Mechanisms of the tropical dominance ",
        "caption": "Figure 10 Open in figure viewer PowerPoint Mechanisms of the tropical dominance and the high correlation between ENSO and CO 2 growth rate. During an El Niño event such as 1997–1998, climate anomalies in most of the tropical land regions change in the same direction, and the anti-correlation between precipitation and temperature “conspire” with plant and soil physiology to produce the large carbon release from the tropical land area.",
